title: Veeam: CDP Jobs
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the state of the Continuous Data Protection (CDP)
 policies of Veeam Backup & Replication. If the policy is not disabled, the
 check also monitors the time since the last long-term restore point. For a
 policy with several replicas, the oldest of their latest long-term restore
 points is used.

 A CDP policy replicates continuously, while long-term restore points are
 created on their own schedule. The time since the last long-term restore
 point therefore does not reflect the RPO, and it also counts long-term
 restore points that Veeam created incomplete.

 In order to carry out the check, the Veeam agent plugin
 needs to be installed on the backup server. See special instructions in the
 comment section of the two Veeam agent plug-in scripts on how to install
 the scripts.

 - The policy state is {OK} if it is {InitialSync}, {Running} or {Disabled},
   {CRIT} if it is {Failed} or {Stopped} and {UNKNOWN} otherwise.

 - The time since the last long-term restore point goes {WARN} if it lies in
   the future.

 You can also configure upper thresholds for the time since the last
 long-term restore point. The defaults are {WARN}: 1 day 6 hours and {CRIT}:
 2 days.

 Older versions of the agent plugin also send other values, which are
 ignored. The oldest versions do not send the time of the last long-term
 restore point. In this case, only the policy state is shown.

discovery:
 One service is created for each CDP job created by the Veeam tool, including
 disabled ones. To leave out disabled jobs, disable this in the rule "Veeam: CDP
 job discovery".

item:
 The name of the CDP job.
